# Layer boundaries

Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md` before changing application code.

## Dependency direction

- `domain/` may depend only on its own domain and pure shared domain primitives.
- `application/` may depend on domain and application-owned ports.
- `infrastructure/` may depend on domain/application to implement ports, but never on UI.
- `ui/` and `src/app/` may invoke application use cases and use presentation contracts, but never import Drizzle, DB connections, repository implementations, or infrastructure adapters.
- Only `src/shared/infrastructure/composition/` may wire concrete dependencies across all layers.

Do not hide a forbidden dependency behind a re-export. Do not move business logic into a page, Server Action, Route Handler, repository, schema, or component.

Create only the folders and ports required by the current vertical; do not scaffold empty layers.
